    "q-72679": {
      "dom_id": "step-q72679",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Simplify the  expression\n$\\frac{n}{{n}^{4}}\\cdot {n}^{8}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First we apply the quotient rule, subtracting exponents in the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{n}{{n}^{4}}\\cdot {n}^{8} & = \\\\ {n}^{1-4}\\cdot {n}^{8} & = \\\\ {n}^{-3}\\cdot {n}^{8} & \\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen we apply the product rule, adding exponents in the product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{n}^{-3}\\cdot {n}^{8} & = \\\\ {n}^{-3+8} & = \\\\ {n}^{5} & \\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{n}{{n}^{4}}\\cdot {n}^{8}={n}^{5}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
