    "q-72682": {
      "dom_id": "step-q72682",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Simplify the  expression\n${q}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{{q}^{3}}{{q}^{8}}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First we apply the quotient rule, subtracting exponents in the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{q}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{{q}^{3}}{{q}^{8}} & = \\\\ {q}^{2}\\cdot {q}^{3-8} & = \\\\ {q}^{2}\\cdot {q}^{-5} & \\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen we apply the product rule, adding exponents in the product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{q}^{2}\\cdot {q}^{-5} & = \\\\ {q}^{2+(-5)} & = \\\\ {q}^{2-5} & = \\\\ {q}^{-3} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{{q}^{3}} & \\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{q}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{{q}^{3}}{{q}^{8}}=\\frac{1}{{q}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
