    "q-72677": {
      "dom_id": "step-q72677",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Simplify ${a}^{5}\\cdot \\frac{{a}^{-3}}{{a}^{2}}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First we apply the quotient rule, subtracting exponents in the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{5}\\cdot \\frac{{a}^{-3}}{{a}^{2}} & = \\\\ {a}^{5}\\cdot {a}^{(-3-2)} & = \\\\ {a}^{5}\\cdot {a}^{-5} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen we apply the product rule, adding exponents in the product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{a}^{5}\\cdot {a}^{-5} & = \\\\ {a}^{5+(-5)} & = \\\\ {a}^{5-5} & = \\\\ {a}^{0} & = \\\\ 1 & \\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{a}^{5}\\cdot \\frac{{a}^{-3}}{{a}^{2}}=1.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
